  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.461pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78.994pt, 256.435pt, "Abstract")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.862pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 275.331pt, "Moiré metasurfaces offer a versatile platform for wavefront engineering through the relative rotation of periodic")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.943pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 289.319pt, "structures. Despite extensive demonstrations of continuous beam steering, the physical mechanisms governing")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.062pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 303.306pt, "beam multiplicity remain poorly understood, hindering the systematic design of multibeam radiation states.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.002pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 317.294pt, "Here, we establish a predictive framework for engineering beam multiplicity in reflective moiré metasurfaces")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.913pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 331.281pt, "based on the dominant Fourier coefficients of their constituent patterns. We reveal that the rotational symmetry")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.062pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 345.269pt, "of these Fourier components in reciprocal space fully determines the symmetry of the resulting moiré unit")
  #line-at(79.37pt, 359.256pt, "cell")
  #line-at(97.235pt, 359.256pt, "and,")
  #line-at(117.64pt, 359.256pt, "consequently,")
  #line-at(175.989pt, 359.256pt, "its")
  #line-at(188.783pt, 359.256pt, "radiation")
  #line-at(228.099pt, 359.256pt, "characteristics.")
  #line-at(291.854pt, 359.256pt, "By")
  #line-at(306.904pt, 359.256pt, "further")
  #line-at(337.989pt, 359.256pt, "incorporating")
  #line-at(396.176pt, 359.256pt, "their")
  #line-at(417.994pt, 359.256pt, "phase")
  #line-at(444.323pt, 359.256pt, "information,")
  #line-at(497.835pt, 359.256pt, "both")
  #line-at(79.37pt, 373.244pt, "beam multiplicity and steering trajectories can be accurately predicted. We demonstrate this approach using")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.047pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 387.232pt, "reflective moiré metasurfaces constructed from patterns with p6m, p3m1, and p4m plane-group symmetries,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.898pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 401.219pt, "achieving one-, two-, three-, four-, and six-beam radiation states with continuously tunable steering trajectories.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.992pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 415.207pt, "Beyond symmetry-based design, we identify two additional degrees of freedom for beam multiplicity control.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.862pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 429.194pt, "Selecting different rotation centers reshapes the phase distributions of the dominant Fourier coefficients, enabling")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.913pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 443.182pt, "further manipulation of beam multiplicity and spatial arrangement, while varying the relative twist angle alters")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.047pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 457.169pt, "the pairing of Fourier components, inducing transitions between distinct beam multiplicities. These findings")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.963pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 471.157pt, "establish a systematic framework for versatile and reconfigurable multibeam wavefront engineering.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.955pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
