#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.018pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78.977pt, 87.495pt, "wavefront")
  #line-at(126.68pt, 87.495pt, "manipulation")
  #line-at(188.992pt, 87.495pt, "[38, 44, 45]")
  #line-at(242.604pt, 87.495pt, "and")
  #line-at(262.254pt, 87.495pt, "polarization-selective")
  #line-at(361.465pt, 87.495pt, "filtering")
  #line-at(400.5pt, 87.495pt, "[46].")
  #line-at(425.403pt, 87.495pt, "Moiré")
  #line-at(456.17pt, 87.495pt, "beamforming")
  #line-at(79.37pt, 103.754pt, "metasurfaces enable reconfigurable wave control solely by adjusting the relative rotation between")
  #line-at(79.37pt, 120.013pt, "two patterned layers, substantially reducing implementation complexity and cost while enhancing")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.953pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 136.272pt, "system robustness [47,48]. These advantages make them an attractive candidate for next-generation")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.018pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78.977pt, 152.531pt, "wireless")
  #line-at(118.991pt, 152.531pt, "communication")
  #line-at(191.774pt, 152.531pt, "systems")
  #line-at(230.119pt, 152.531pt, "and")
  #line-at(249.736pt, 152.531pt, "a")
  #line-at(258.226pt, 152.531pt, "potential")
  #line-at(300.721pt, 152.531pt, "alternative")
  #line-at(351.072pt, 152.531pt, "to")
  #line-at(363.279pt, 152.531pt, "reconfigurable")
  #line-at(431.1pt, 152.531pt, "intelligent")
  #line-at(479.503pt, 152.531pt, "surfaces")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.909pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.01pt, 168.79pt, "(RISs) [49,50].")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.018pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.552pt, 185.049pt, "In 2022, we initially proposed a reflective moiré metasurface for steering the reflected wave to")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.849pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 201.308pt, "symmetric directions [51]. Distinct from previous moiré metasurfaces based on either thick dielectric")
  #line-at(79.37pt, 217.566pt, "structures or cascaded configurations, our reflective moiré metasurface employs a zero-spacing moiré")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.018pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 233.825pt, "pattern")
  #line-at(114.588pt, 233.825pt, "formed")
  #line-at(150.596pt, 233.825pt, "by")
  #line-at(165.495pt, 233.825pt, "two")
  #line-at(185.903pt, 233.825pt, "metallic")
  #line-at(225.85pt, 233.825pt, "layers,")
  #line-at(258.586pt, 233.825pt, "thereby")
  #line-at(295.729pt, 233.825pt, "effectively")
  #line-at(346.013pt, 233.825pt, "reducing")
  #line-at(389.042pt, 233.825pt, "the")
  #line-at(406.735pt, 233.825pt, "overall")
  #line-at(440.973pt, 233.825pt, "device")
  #line-at(473.832pt, 233.825pt, "thickness.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.799pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 250.084pt, "However, similar to other reported studies on moiré metasurfaces [15,52,53], our previously proposed")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.964pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 266.343pt, "reflective moiré metasurfaces were restricted to four- and six-beam radiation patterns, limiting their")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.904pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 282.602pt, "adaptability in communication and sensing applications. In addition, previous studies have primarily")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.81pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 298.861pt, "focused on predicting beam trajectories through reciprocal-space vector analysis [51")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.909pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(439.852pt, 298.861pt, "–")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.81pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(445.307pt, 298.861pt, "55], whereas the")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.958pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 315.12pt, "physical principles governing beam multiplicity have received little attention. More specifically, the")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.936pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 331.379pt, "relationship between different combinations of periodic patterns and the resulting beam multiplicity")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.909pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 347.638pt, "remains unclear.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.012pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.552pt, 363.897pt, "Here, we establish a predictive framework for engineering beam multiplicity in reflective moiré")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.799pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 380.156pt, "metasurfaces based on Fourier-coefficient phase synthesis. We show that the phase distributions of moiré")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.964pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 396.415pt, "components, synthesized from the dominant Fourier components of constituent patterns, determine")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.821pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 412.674pt, "the number of radiated beams. Using patterns with p6m, p3m1, and p4m plane-group symmetries, we")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.799pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 428.933pt, "realize one-, two-, three-, four-, and six-beam radiation states, covering all rotational orders allowed by")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.843pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 445.192pt, "crystallographic symmetry in two-dimensional periodic systems. Beyond symmetry-based design, we")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.799pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 461.451pt, "identify two additional degrees of freedom for beam multiplicity control: rotation-center selection and")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 477.71pt, "relative twist-angle adjustment. Selecting different rotation centers alters the phases of the dominant")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.018pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 493.969pt, "Fourier coefficients, thereby reshaping the synthesized phase distributions and resulting radiation")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.799pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 510.228pt, "states. In contrast, varying the relative twist angle changes the pairing of Fourier components, enabling")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.964pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.37pt, 526.487pt, "transitions between distinct beam multiplicities. The resulting far-field radiation patterns agree well")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.018pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78.977pt, 542.746pt, "with")
  #line-at(102.3pt, 542.746pt, "theoretical")
  #line-at(152.807pt, 542.746pt, "predictions.")
  #line-at(208.588pt, 542.746pt, "This")
  #line-at(231.91pt, 542.746pt, "framework")
  #line-at(283.563pt, 542.746pt, "establishes")
  #line-at(335.149pt, 542.746pt, "a")
  #line-at(343.628pt, 542.746pt, "direct")
  #line-at(372.515pt, 542.746pt, "link")
  #line-at(393.367pt, 542.746pt, "between")
  #line-at(433.659pt, 542.746pt, "Fourier-coefficient")
